# Google Search Console Report - 2026-08-23

> **DATE CORRECTION (2026-08-23).** Written stamped `2026-08-17`; the actual run date is **2026-08-23**, verified against the system clock. Data below is correct as read live on 2026-08-23. **Filename needs renaming to `GSC_Report_2026-08-23.md`.** Note the GSC window genuinely ended 15 Aug, so the search data lags the run date by about a week.

**Property:** https://www.masteringobservability.com/ (URL-prefix). Read live via browser, no re-authentication wall.
**Window:** rolling 3 months, 16 May to 15 Aug 2026.
**Baseline for comparison:** `02_SEARCH_CONSOLE_BASELINE.md` (49 clicks, 9,880 impressions, 0.5% CTR, avg position 19.5, 2026-03-20 to 06-19).

---

## Site totals

| Metric | 2026-08-17 | 2026-08-10 | 2026-08-03 | Baseline |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Total clicks | **53** | 51 | 48 | 49 |
| Total impressions | **5,950** | 5,990 | 6,169 | 9,880 |
| Average CTR | **0.9%** | 0.9% | 0.8% | 0.5% |
| Average position | **27.3** | 26.7 | 25.9 | 19.5 |
| Queries | **286** | 272 | 254 | 261 |

Clicks up 2 and CTR holding at 0.9%, which is nearly double baseline. Impressions flat and position drifting 0.6 further out. The query surface widened again (254, 272, 286 across three runs), which is the mechanism behind the worsening average position: the site is matching more terms, most of them at poor ranks.

